(*
  X-Wing computational-model proof — TEMPLATE / POINTER, not a runnable model.

  ProVerif (verification/proverif/*.pv) proves the handshake in the SYMBOLIC
  model: it treats ML-KEM and X25519 as perfect black boxes. CryptoVerif proves
  security in the COMPUTATIONAL model instead — a sequence of game hops that
  bounds the adversary's advantage by reductions to the underlying hardness
  assumptions (IND-CCA of ML-KEM, Gap-DH of X25519). That is strictly stronger.

  We do NOT re-derive it here because X-Wing already has a published, peer-
  reviewed computational proof of its combiner:

    Barbosa, Connolly, Duarte, Kaiser, Schwabe, Varner, Westerbaan,
    "X-Wing: The Hybrid KEM You've Been Looking For", IACR CiC 2024/1.
    Theorem: X-Wing is IND-CCA secure if ML-KEM-768 is IND-CCA secure and
    X25519 satisfies the Gap-DH assumption (in the ROM/QROM for SHA3-256).

  To reproduce the combiner game locally once CryptoVerif is installed:
    1. Model the two KEMs with CryptoVerif's `Kem` / DH primitive libraries.
    2. Model `combine = SHA3-256(label || ss_m || ss_x || ct_x || pk_x)` as a
       random oracle (ROM).
    3. Assert `Secrecy(K)` and run: cryptoverif xwing.ocv
       -> expect "RESULT Proved secrecy of K".

  Rationale for pointing rather than re-proving: a hand-rolled computational
  proof that disagrees with the published one would be a liability, not an asset.
  The citation IS the verification at this layer; this file records how to
  reproduce it if required.
*)
